    <span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Vietnam Rental Guide</span>
    <h1>Hanoi Motorbike Traffic Rules: What Riders Should Know</h1>
    <p>Riding a motorbike in Hanoi is the fastest way to understand the city, and the fastest way to misunderstand it is to assume its traffic works like the traffic at home. It does not. Hanoi's streets run on a fluid, negotiated order that has its own logic, its own habits and, underneath all of it, formal rules that apply to every rider. Visitors who learn both layers, the written rules and the living rhythm, ride more safely and enjoy it more. This guide describes the general picture honestly, with the firm caveat that traffic law changes, and current official sources must always be consulted for anything that matters.</p>
    <p>This article belongs to the <a href="/renting-a-motorbike-in-vietnam/">renting a motorbike in Vietnam</a> hub, which gathers the practical guidance for riding in this country. For licensing questions specifically, read the <a href="/renting-a-motorbike-in-vietnam/motorbike-license-vietnam-tourists/">license guide for tourists</a>, and for the machines themselves, start at the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> hub. Nothing here is legal advice; it is a rider's orientation.</p>

    <nav class="toc" aria-label="Table of contents">
      <p>On this page</p>
      <ol>
        <li><a href="#sec-1">The written rules and the living rhythm</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-2">The core rules every rider must respect</a></li>
